# ZylCode line-ending and diff normalisation
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# ---------------
# This repository is developed on Windows (primary target platform) with
# `core.autocrlf=true` and, until now, no `.gitattributes`.
#
# Consequence observed on 2026-09-17: touching a single line in a file could
# inflate the diff, and the working tree carried ~670 lines of pure
# whitespace/formatting churn across 52 modified files (16% of all insertions).
# That churn obscures real review signal and makes the dirty tree impossible to
# attribute. See docs/governance/STATUS_SWEEP_2026-09-16.md §15.
#
# RULE: normalise to LF in the repository, always. Let the working tree be
# whatever the platform prefers. Reviewers see semantic diffs, not EOL noise.

# Default: text files checked in with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# --- Source code -----------------------------------------------------------
*.rs    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf

# --- Documentation: normalise, and treat as prose for diff purposes --------
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# --- Windows launchers: MUST stay CRLF or cmd.exe misparses them -----------
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# --- Binary: never touch, never diff --------------------------------------
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.db    binary
*.db.bak binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary

# --- Generated / vendored: collapse in diffs and file listings ------------
target/            export-ignore
node_modules/      export-ignore
*.lock             -diff linguist-generated
Cargo.lock         -diff linguist-generated
pnpm-lock.yaml     -diff linguist-generated

# --- Evidence artifacts: keep visible in diffs, but mark as generated -----
docs/governance/** linguist-documentation
